**Hook change logged.** 09 winner was "10 weeks on simple tasks. The store still isn't live." (14/14). Improved to "10 weeks on simple setup tasks. My store still isn't live." because (1) No-Questions: "simple tasks" of what? "setup" names the object and pins the angle; (2) the note is his own handwriting, so "My store" (first person) replaces "The store" and removes the which-store question. Re-scored: S ✓ NQ ✓ F ✓ B ✓ · SC 2 PL 2 SP 2 V 2 EC 2 SS 2 VIS 2 = **14/14**. "simple" is his complaint, never our promise (DNS-08 n/a, as P1 ruled). Stem `10 weeks on` unique in the batch.

**VOC trace (A9):** hook from harvested phrases Q-F-0013 + Q-O-0014 ✓ · subhead reuses "someone ... build" (Q-F-0018), "hire/to do the store for you" meaning (Q-Y-0035) and "live" (Q-O-0014) ✓ · body reuses "set up" (Q-F-0012) ✓ · CTA reuses "live" (Q-O-0014) and "stuck" (Q-F-0014, Q-F-0011) ✓ → hook + 3 other parts carry harvested words.

**Why this belief order (S2 lane).** Subhead names the mechanism first (the builder's job ends the day it goes live); body line 1 is the after-launch handle (PT-04 page words), line 2 the staged tests, and the build claim comes last, phrased as ownership ("Built in your name"), never as "we build your entire store / skip the setup" (DNS-19).

