### Gates
- **Stranger Test: PASS** · in 0.8 s: who = someone setting up their own online store; what = ten weeks and it still isn't live; why = the weeks lost, in his own handwriting.
- **No-Questions Test: PASS** · hook (tasks = setup tasks, store = my store) · subhead ("it" = my store; "builders" named; "the real work" is spelled out by body line 1) · body (every line has its object: review/corrections/products; products/stages/budget; store in your name/listings/shipping) · proof (source named, "the store" named) · CTA (live = the store; stuck = in setup).
- **Familiarity Test: PASS** · verbatim Q-F-0013 + Q-O-0014 wording; "that's me" for anyone in week N of the settings.
- **Aha Test: PASS** · subhead = what he believes/tried (someone builds it, setup fixed) → why it fails (builders leave the day it goes live, M-1) → what's needed (someone for the work that starts then).
- **So-What Test: PASS** · each body line is a benefit with a because: not left alone after launch · no single-guess spend, you approve the budget · the store is yours and set up without the weeks in settings.
- **Squint Test: PASS (by spec)** · only the hand-lettered hook exceeds 1/10 of canvas height; verify on render.
- **Phone Test: PASS (by spec)** · smallest string (proof) specified at ≥3% canvas height (≈32 px at 1080); verify at feed size on render.

